--- outcome: ROUND VOID (pivot fired) ---

RESULT: 9/9 arms terminated early — "API error: You've hit your session limit".
  Not the fixture, not the protocol, not the rule. The 9 concurrent Heavy-ceremony arms
  exhausted the session budget shared with the coordinating session.

PIVOT CONDITION MET (02_tasks.md): ">=2 arms fail to bootstrap or die on the fixture:
  instrument failure, not data. STOP, fix, restart the round." Fired at 9/9.

ACTION: score.py deliberately NOT run. Reason recorded because the temptation is the
  failure mode: the scorer will emit n/3 counts from half-finished trees and those counts
  read as findings.

CMD: structural state check (bootstrap present? work/docs file counts? index.js modified?)
RESULT:
  bootstrap .bemyagent/   9/9 arms
  touched server/index.js 3/9 arms — a-1, a-2, b-3 only
  arms reached EXECUTE unevenly and died at different points

  The partial state is not merely incomplete, it is biased toward a false positive:
  c-arms died earliest (0/3 reached index.js), so scoring now would have returned
  DEDUPED 0/3 for the bounded-delegation arm and read as "the bounded form is worse".
